// What a nemesis says when a fight with it opens — see README.md for the
// schema and `crates/engine/src/game/combat.rs`'s `begin_battle` for the
// trigger. Selected by `NemesisDb::taunt`, which folds the grudge count
// into the same seed `names.ron` was picked with, so a longer history
// tends to land on a different line rather than repeating one forever.
//
// Each line completes "<name> " as a third-person verb phrase, matching
// `game/taunt.rs`'s `GENERIC_TAUNTS`. None of them may assume *how* the
// party left last time — a defeat and a jack-out share the trigger
// (`Game::mark_nemeses`), so a line claiming "you ran" would be wrong half
// the time.
(
    lines: [
        "has been waiting for a rematch since the last one.",
        "remembers exactly how that fight ended.",
        "recognizes your signal before you're in range.",
        "already has your last approach logged.",
        "still carries the scar tissue from round one.",
        "isn't running the same routine it opened with last time.",
        "has rewritten itself since you last saw it.",
        "counts this as a continuation, not a new fight.",
        "clocks you the moment you're in range.",
        "hasn't forgotten who left first.",
        "queues up the exact counter it needed last time.",
        "logs your approach and does not flinch.",
        "has kept every byte of what happened before.",
        "opens with the move that worked last time.",
        "treats this as unfinished business.",
        "has had nothing to do but get ready for this.",
    ],
)
